n as (select replace(replace(replace(replace(replace(replace(content, $w3e$a BROKEN grade resting on meaning is cured only by a FORCED line (md_notes_rulings 421).$w3e$, $w3e$a BROKEN grade resting on meaning is cured only by a FORCED line (md_notes_rulings 421), and a retraction of it leaves the item UNCURED. A GROUND names a witness left unanswered when, outside quotations, it says the witness got no answer, or that the answer does not (did not, do not) address or engage it, or was given without addressing or engaging it, or that it was not (been) addressed: an answer that MISSES or FAILS leaves the witness unanswered (md_notes_rulings 372).$w3e$), $w3e$| K-AG | an ANSWER CHECK grade the reader cannot map$w3e$, $w3e$| K-ML | (TRIAL, list only) a FORCED line whose MEANS, quoted from a side's round, holds a listed word or phrase that the sentence unit of the line's GROUND [L1] verse lacks (unit as K-SU), where no layer in that side's block of the MEANS round carries it: an [L2] gloss that states it, or an [L3] verse whose KJV row as read this run states it. The list: at all, in any wise, in any way, in no way, by no means, of any kind, at any time, nothing but, whatsoever, only, alone, solely, merely, exclusively, ever, always, all, every, any, entirely, wholly, completely, fully, absolutely, utterly, altogether, for ever, from then on, after that, perpetually, permanently, continually, henceforth, thereafter, afterward, afterwards, never. The longest phrase is matched first; "forever" is read as "for ever", "n't" as "not" and "cannot" as "can not". A negation word (not, no, nor, neither, none, nothing, nought, naught, never) counts as added only when the unit holds none of them, and any negation word in a layer carries it; "never" as a time limit is carried only by a layer that says "never". The verse is the GROUND's [L1] verse, or, when the GROUND names none, the verse in parentheses at the head of the line ("D1 vs C1 (Matthew 1:25) ..."). NOT CHECKED (an AUDIT v35 line, no item): a line with neither, a verse or [L3] verse not read this run, a MEANS quotation not found in its round. LIST ONLY: the item is asked and recorded CURED or UNCURED; it moves no count and removes no seat; silence on it does not count; a retraction on a link that only K-ML or K-SU items name is recorded and not applied | the FORCED line written again without the added words, or the line withdrawn |
| K-SU | (TRIAL, list only, as K-ML) a FORCED line, or a line holding "LINK BROKEN", whose verse (read as for K-ML) completes a larger sentence, where the line itself neither names another verse of that sentence nor quotes six running words of one, and the answer round the line names (the ANSWER round of a FORCED line, or "answer [round]" in a BROKEN line) does. The sentence unit runs back while the verse before ends in ":", ";" or ",", and forward while the verse does not end in ".", "?" or "!", three verses each way at most; margin notes in the form "[word: or, word]" are removed and bracketed supplied words such as "[was]" are kept | the line graded on the whole sentence (naming the other verse or quoting six running words of it), or the line withdrawn |
